# generated by run.sh / manual scans (the runner copies fixtures to a tmpdir, but manual runs write here)
**/.candor/
**/out/
*.class
.part-run.*.sh
# The preflight's conformance-reuse stamp: which SHAs were green, so the next invocation can tell
# whether anything that could change the answer moved. A LOCAL cache, never an artifact — and it must be
# ignored, because an untracked file here makes the tree dirty and a dirty tree correctly forbids reuse.
# The stamp would otherwise defeat itself on its own first write.
.last-green-shas
